<p>
  This policy describes how <%= cream_operator_name %> handles personal information in Cream, our corporate CRM.
  It applies to users invited by their organization and to the data they manage on the platform.
</p>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Data we process</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
    <li>Account data: name, email address and authentication identifiers.</li>
    <li>Usage data: technical logs, IP address and activity needed to operate and secure the service.</li>
    <li>CRM data entered by your team: contacts, companies, deals, notes, tasks and communications.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    We use this data to provide Cream, authenticate users, maintain security, improve the product
    and meet legal obligations. AI features, when enabled in your workspace,
    process only the information required for the requested action.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Retention and access</h2>
  <p>
    Data is kept while your organization maintains the service or as required by law.
    Access is limited to authorized <%= cream_operator_name %> staff with an operational need. We do not sell personal data.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Integrations</h2>
  <p>
    If you connect external services (e.g. Gmail, Stripe or Slack), Cream exchanges only the information
    required for that integration, according to the permissions you grant.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access, correction or deletion of your personal data by contacting
    <%= mail_to cream_privacy_email, cream_privacy_email, class: "text-accent hover:underline" %>.
    Requests about customer or contact data in the CRM should go through your workspace administrator.
  </p>
</section>
